  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Border Security for Countering Transnational Threats Including Movement of Illicit Goods and Violent Extremism in CAR, Kenya, Madagascar, Namibia, and Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project responds to the call to build national border-security capacity in key African jurisdictions of Central African Republic (CAR), Kenya, Madagascar, Namibia, and Somalia, with a goal of addressing complex cross-border security challenges including movement of illicit goods, foreign terrorist fighters, and transfers of proliferation-related expertise, materiel and financing by organized criminal groups, violent extremist organizations and associated smuggling networks. The project will enhance border-management systems and capacities to support compliance with international standards and, to the extent possible, interoperability with commonly used international platforms.</narrative>
  </description>
